#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Noise Modeling {#noise-modeling}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A noise model describes how errors affect the results from executing a "
"quantum circuit. Noise models support several stages of a typical workflow "
"including: simulating a circuit classically to estimate expected performance"
" before submitting a job  or to inform an error-mitigation technique such as"
" probabilistic error cancellation. For general strategies to reduce the "
"impact of noise during execution, see [Overview of noise management "
"techniques](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This page collects the packages and capabilities that support each part of "
"that workflow, grouped into learning noise from a device, building a noise "
"model for classical simulation, and refining a noise model for a specific "
"error-mitigation technique.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Building and running noise learning algorithms {#building-and-running-noise-"
"learning-algorithms}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use noise learning packages to characterize a device's noise directly from "
"experimental data. These packages run randomized circuits to estimate error "
"rates and build a noise model that reflects actual hardware behavior.\n"
msgstr ""

